### Recommendation for Vite Deployment
To ensure `process.env.API_KEY` works correctly in your Vite-powered browser app (since `process` is a Node.js global not available in browsers by default), you should add this to your `vite.config.ts`:

```javascript
import { defineConfig } from 'vite'

export default defineConfig({
  // ... other config
  define: {
    'process.env.API_KEY': JSON.stringify(process.env.VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY)
  }
})
```

This will automatically map your `VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY` to the `process.env.API_KEY` variable that the Gemini SDK expects, resolving the "An API Key must be set" error without violating the integration guidelines.
